--- !u!114 &1214643522
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1214643517}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1d93b10eeeb25d24ca6a0bcf619655e5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Tutorial
  parentObjectUI: {fileID: 1253557475}
  tutorialText: {fileID: 1623167372}
  walkDistanceMarginal: 0.02
  target1: {x: -5.7, y: -0.64, z: 0}
  playerMoveSpeed: 1
  wolfPrefab: {fileID: 5679632090492468569, guid: fb72abb249b95c2498c62bb1a5226967, type: 3}
  wolfOffset: {x: 0, y: 7}
  texts1:
  - Hello! Welcome to your very own farm, the place you'll be spending the next couple
    of weeks.
  - You will need to venture out into the wild to collect valuable materials such
    as stone and wood. But you won't have to do it alone.
  - There's a lot of little guys living on your farm alongside you. Talk to them
    at the start of each day to recruit them to your expedition, but don't bring
    too many or too few.
  - Try recruiting 3 little guys, no more and no less.
  texts2:
  - Now you have 5 little guys following you, that should be more than enough.
  - In fact, it may be too much. Go ahead and unrecruit 2 of them so that you're
    only bringing 3 of them with you.
  texts3:
  - Congratulations, you now have 5 little guys following you! The rest of the little
    guys will stay at the farm and bake bread for the next day. The amount of bread
    you have decides how many little guys you can bring with you.
  - The day technically hasn't really started until you open the gates to your farm.
    The amount of little guys following you and the amount staying at home are locked
    for the rest of the day once you open the gates.
  - I think it's time to head out into the wild, the gates are located right above
    where you started.
  texts4:
  - 'At the start of each day you will get a mission. It will be a goal of how many
    materials you need to get. '
  - You might have noticed, and maybe even clicked on, the arrow at the bottom of
    the screen. It shows you your current mission and progress towards it.
  - Go collect what you need to reach its demands. The more little guys you have
    with you, the faster you will mine resources.
  - You can also leave a little guy to mine alone, but they are very slow at it.
  texts5:
  - Well done! As yoo probably noticed, your little guys pick up the materials that
    you mine and bring them back to the barn.
  - 'With them leaving your actions become weaker as you mine. '
  - Let's head back to the farm, you need to be there before the day ends.
  texts6:
  - Oh no! Looks like a wolf is coming this way.
  - You're going to have to fight it off!
  texts7:
  - 'Wow, that was really impressive! '
  - Wolves are going to be a big hurdle for you to tackle. They live in caves which
    means that you will have to destroy their cave if you want to stop them... Or
    you could just try to ignore them.
  - As I mentioned earlier, the more little guys you have, the more powerful you
    are.
  - Good luck!
  cutscene: 0
  canOpenGates: 0
